    "MEDICATIONS": {
      "present": true,
      "status": "content",
      "content_blocks": [],
      "subsections": {
        "DRUG(S) OF CHOICE": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "DRUG(S) OF CHOICE",
          "canonical_heading": "DRUG(S) OF CHOICE",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "If micro- or macrovascular thromboembolic complications are suspected, antiplatelet agents (e.g., clopidogrel, aspirin) may be indicated, although their use in humans with thrombocytosis has been associated with more severe hemorrhagic complications. Consultation with a veterinary specialist is highly recommended to determine if and which therapy may be indicated.",
              "pdf_page": 1413,
              "printed_page": 1331,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Hydroxyurea is a chemotherapy drug that is used for cytoreductive therapy in humans with essential thrombocytosis. Published dosage recommendations for veterinary species vary widely. It is generally myelo suppressive, however, and will affect all cell lines. Consultation with a veterinary specialist is recommended regarding the administration and dosage of this drug. A comprehensive CBC every 1–2 weeks is recommended while taking hydroxyurea until platelet count stabilizes. Regular assessment of a serum biochemical profile is also recommended if using this drug.",
              "pdf_page": 1413,
              "printed_page": 1331,
              "column": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "CONTRAINDICATIONS": {
          "present": false,
          "status": "missing",
          "source_heading": null,
          "canonical_heading": "CONTRAINDICATIONS",
          "content_blocks": []
        },
        "PRECAUTIONS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "PRECAUTIONS",
          "canonical_heading": "PRECAUTIONS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Concurrent use of hydroxyurea with other bone marrow depressant drugs may cause additive myelosuppression; use with caution.",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
        "POSSIBLE INTERACTIONS": {
          "present": false,
          "status": "missing",
          "source_heading": null,
          "canonical_heading": "POSSIBLE INTERACTIONS",
          "content_blocks": []
        },
        "CONTRAINDICATIONS/POSSIBLE INTERACTIONS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "CONTRAINDICATIONS/POSSIBLE INTERACTIONS",
          "canonical_heading": "CONTRAINDICATIONS/POSSIBLE INTERACTIONS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Caution is recommended for the use of hydroxyurea in patients with anemia, preexisting bone marrow depression, history of urate stones, current infection, impaired",
              "pdf_page": 1413,
              "printed_page": 1331,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "renal function, or with previous chemother apy or radiation therapy.",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "subheading",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Adverse Effects",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Gastrointestinal effects of hydroxyurea may",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Adverse Effects"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "include anorexia, vomiting, or diarrhea.",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Adverse Effects"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Additional adverse effects include",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Adverse Effects"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "stomatitis, sloughing of toenails, loss of fur,",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Adverse Effects"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "and dysuria.",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Adverse Effects"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Bone marrow supression (anemia,",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Adverse Effects"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "thrombocytopenia, leukopenia) and lung",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Adverse Effects"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "damage (pulmonary fibrosis) are the most",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Adverse Effects"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "serious potential adverse effects of hydroxyurea.",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Adverse Effects"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Therapy should be discontinued until values",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Adverse Effects"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "return to normal.",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Adverse Effects"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Life-threatening methemoglobinemia has",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Adverse Effects"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "been reported in cats given high dosages",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Adverse Effects"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "(>500 mg) of hydroxyurea.",
              "pdf_page": 1414,
              "printed_page": 1332,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Adverse Effects"
            }
          ]
        },
